## 席位核对

**L1 first review (full) · REWORK, paper only** · Head-sha: `ef48f915c84c2351059d49b6187b4abb58df8c44` · card #34613 (`Fixes #34613`) · read 2026-11-17T13:13Z

There is no earlier L1 record. Contract review FAIL 6946116756 was at `c67cb4c0`. Inputs:
- card body, ruling B 6942780880, claim round 2 6943123938, hand-off 6948327012, takeover 6948809548 and correction 6948830311;
- the PR body;
- the net diff from merge-base `3bbda33b` (79 files, +1104 / -502);
- check-runs on this head.

Both open findings are text fixes and need no code change. The code reads correct.

### Must-fix

**M1. 30 or so paths fall outside the claimed file surface, and the card has no amendment for them.** Claim 6943123938 names:
- `seed.zod.ts` and its tests;
- `seed-loader.ts`;
- `protocol-save-door-refusals.ts`;
- `validate-seed-replay-safety`;
- the conversion route, the migration entry, the regenerated spec artefacts, docs and the root changeset;

and it says "Stop and report on a breach". The diff also moves these:
- `packages/metadata/src/artifact-retired-seed-modes.ts` (new) and its test, and `packages/metadata/src/plugin.ts` (the L2 M1 fix);
- `packages/runtime/src/app-plugin.ts` and `packages/cloud-connection/src/marketplace-install-local-plugin.ts` (the `loadStored` callers);
- `packages/cli/src/commands/diff.ts`;
- `packages/metadata-core/src/package-upgrade-plan.ts` (jsdoc);
- `packages/spec/src/data/seed-loader.zod.ts` (jsdoc);
- `packages/lint/src/authoring-rules.ts`, `index.ts` and `rule-explanations.ts`;
- `scripts/check-skill-identifier-liveness.mjs` and `scripts/engine-double-contract.pinned.json`;
- existing tests outside the named surface:
  - 13 `metadata-protocol/src/seed-loader-*.test.ts`, plus `protocol.seed-external-id-refusal` and `protocol-publish-drafts-all-or-nothing`;
  - 13 `cloud-connection` install-local tests;
  - in `runtime`: `app-plugin.seed*`, `artifact-collections`, `bulk-write-real-driver`, `seed-datasets`, `seed-loader*`;
  - `cli/test/diff-upgrade-plan` and `seed-record-values-load-parity`;
  - `objectql/src/engine-seed-required-deferral`, `verify/src/harness.seed-temporal-form` and dogfood `grant-table-write-contract`.

Each looks forced: by the L2 M1/S1 fixes, by the removed enum members, or by a gate. The PR body explains most of them. Please post one claim amendment on #34613 that lists these paths with their reasons. The card thread is gone, so area o3-J posts it. A delta ACCEPT on this same head follows once it is up.

### Should-fix

**S1. The changeset's `Skills-docs:` line still says the follow-up is owed, but the card is filed.** `.changeset/34613-…md` reads `Skills-docs: follow-up owed — skills/objectstack-data/references/seeds.md, skills/objectstack-platform/SKILL.md`. #34798 is filed and open, and the PR body already says `follow-up #34798`. Rewrite the changeset line to `follow-up #34798` so the published changelog and the body agree. One line. It moves the head, so CI reruns and a delta read follows.

### Nits (each may become its own card under the small-flaw rule; neither blocks)

- **N1.** The changeset does not name the new export `RETIRED_SEED_MODE_VALUES` (`@objectstack/spec/data`, `api-surface/data.json` +1 row). The PR body does name it. If S1's edit touches the changeset anyway, adding a clause there closes this nit with no card.
- **N2.** `packages/metadata/src/plugin.ts` computes the artifact `checksum` from the parsed definition before `restoreWithheldSeedDatasets` hands the withheld dataset back into the same object. The checksum therefore covers the artifact without that dataset. Nothing reads the dataset except the seed load, which refuses it, so no answer changes. Recorded only.

### Checklist (the rest holds)

- **Shape:** Draft against `main`, `mergeable_state: clean`. The only closing keyword is `Fixes #34613`, and the card's whole ask is this retirement. Title is `fix(spec,metadata-protocol)!`.
- **Ruling B (6942780880), executed as ruled:**
  - `SeedMode` keeps `update | upsert | ignore`, default `ignore`.
  - `insert` and `replace` are retired values through `enumWithRetiredValues`, with a prescription that names the fix.
  - Both hints are repointed: `seed-loader.ts:1739-1740`, and the save door's in `protocol-save-door-refusals.ts`.
  - The lint rule is removed (69 → 68, transcripts follow).
  - The conversion route ships in the same PR (`seed-data.mdx` › *Moving off `insert` and `replace`*).
  - The ADR-0087 D3 entry `seed-mode-insert-replace-retired` is registered.
  - The `18.6.0` in the prescriptions is the next minor of `@objectstack/spec` 18.5.0.
- **L2 6946116756 M1 is closed.** A compiled artifact with a retired-mode dataset no longer aborts the boot. `withholdRetiredSeedModes` takes such datasets out of every seed collection path (top-level and `manifest` `data`, and each `packages[i]` and `packages[i].manifest`) before the strict parse, without mutating the input. `restoreWithheldSeedDatasets` hands them back after the parse. A never-valid mode is still the parse's refusal. The fix is pinned by a real `createStandaloneStack` boot (3 cases, a `merge` CONTROL included) and 3 unit cases.
- **L2 S1 is closed.** `loadDataset` refuses any mode outside the live `SeedMode` set before any write: nothing is written, every record counts as errored, the schema's prescription is the error, and it is logged at `error`. The `insert` / `replace` arms are gone from `writeRecord` and `decideWriteAction`, and a request with no mode keeps its old path. Pinned by `seed-loader-retired-mode-34613.test.ts` (8 cases, with CONTROLs).
- **The "refused alone" funnel.** `SeedLoaderService.loadStored` refuses only a dataset whose mode is a retired value. Every other malformation still throws from the request parse, and an all-refused load answers the failed empty result. Its product callers are the boot seed, the per-organization replay and the dev hot reload (`app-plugin.ts:2066`, `:2170`, `:2660`) and the marketplace local install (`marketplace-install-local-plugin.ts:7674`). The two other `SeedLoaderService` constructions (`protocol-publish-batch.ts:107` and `runtime/src/domains/packages.ts:5089`) apply just-published seeds, with the author present, and keep the whole-request 422 as the body says.
- **Docs made false:** I grepped `content/docs`, `packages`, `examples` and the spec `.describe()` text for `mode: 'insert' | 'replace'`. Every remaining hit is historical ("retired", "once"), or another `mode` (`permissions/authentication.mdx:1276`, the user import's `insert | upsert`; the engine's `'insert' | 'update'` write kinds). The `SeedSchema.mode` describe now says "Every mode matches on `externalId`", which is true of the three live modes. Skills: `seeds.md` and `platform/SKILL.md` still teach the retired modes. #34798 carries that, `Blocked-by` this card.
- **Changeset:** It names spec, metadata-protocol and lint as `minor` (`Metadata-protocol: narrowed` requires at least `minor`), and runtime, cloud-connection, cli and metadata as `patch`. `@objectstack/metadata-core` (jsdoc only) is not named. It is in the same `fixed` group in `.changeset/config.json`, so its version moves with the rest, and `Check Changeset` is `success`. The FROM/TO lines match the code. "Unchanged: `ignore`, `upsert` and `update` datasets load byte-identically" agrees with the diff, which only removes arms and adds the refusal ahead of them.
- **Tests:** there are 14 new cases across the three new files. The existing-test edits follow the removed members, and each I sampled replaced `insert` with a keyed mode, which is the PR's own prescription. Real-boot FROM/TO readings are in the body.
- **Narrowing evidence:** the body does not report a dogfood battery pinned to `ef48f915`. The dogfood check-runs on this head were skipped by path filter, and the `grant-table-write-contract` dogfood test is listed as green locally. Per the checklist, a narrowing needs a full battery on the head before it is queued. I am flagging this for the landing step, not as a finding at this L1.
- **Gates at this head:** 74 check-runs, all completed: 62 `success` and 12 `skipped`, none failed. The `Test UI (15/16)` red named in the hand-off is `success` on its rerun.

### Owed after this (nothing here readies, queues or arms the PR)

- The area posts the claim amendment (M1). S1 is a one-line changeset edit, then a delta read.
- **Seat L2 delta at `CONTRACT_REVIEW_TIER`** on `c67cb4c0..ef48f915`: the faces are a narrowing of `packages/spec/src` and a new published export (`RETIRED_SEED_MODE_VALUES`). The L2 M1 and S1 fixes need the reviewer's own close.
- **Ruling B step 3 precondition, for the seat:** the hosted stock of `insert` / `replace` datasets is unknown (source side zero, per the cloud seat's reading). The ruling has the count reported on the card before landing. Tier H waits on that count, or on the maintainer accepting the unknown.
- **Tier H:** the PR narrows `packages/spec/src`, so os-zhuang must approve on the final head, and a full dogfood battery must be pinned to it.
- Note, no change asked: the body still opens with seat 2's attribution lines and ends with its signed trailer.
